<title>USA: U.S. 5-year note auction high yield 6.165 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. 5-year note auction high yield 6.165 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Treasury said its Dutch bidding auction of 5-year notes produced these results:</p>
<p>			 5-YEAR NOTES DUE DEC 31, 2001</p>
<p>			     $12.508 BILLION AUCTION</p>
<p>	     YIELD			  PRICE	COUPON</p>
<p> HIGH	6.165    Awarded At	99.830	6.125</p>
<p> MEDIAN    6.150    High Yield	NOT GIVEN  Percent</p>
<p> LOW	 6.110    27 Percent	NOT GIVEN</p>
<p>	   Cover - (Bids Over Amount Sold)    =  2.79 Times</p>
<p> U.S. TREASURY (GOVERNMENT DEBT)		 MATURITY 31.Dec.01</p>
<p> MATURITY/TYPE    5-YEAR NOTES		   PAY DATE 31.Dec.96</p>
<p> TYPE OF DEBT     STRAIGHT			 LAUNCHED 19.Dec.96</p>
<p> ISSUED/ACCEPTED  12.508 BLN USD		 CUSIP    9128272E1</p>
<p> BIDS SUBMITTED   34.899			   COUNTRY	  USA</p>
<p> NONCOMPETITIVE   412.00 MLN			  DUTCH AUCTION</p>
<p> NY FED DISTRICT    N.A.			   COUPON	 6.125</p>
<p> FOREIGN INSTITN  850.00 MLN		     PRICE	 99.830</p>
<p> BIDDING RANGE    6.110-6.165 PCT		YIELD-HIGH   6.165</p>
<p>KEY (HIGH) YIELD UP FROM 5.95 PCT AT AUCTION ON 20.NOV.96</p>
<p>KEY (HIGH) YIELD HIGHEST SINCE 6.325 PCT AT AUCTION 23.OCT.96</p>
